      "text": "`Statevector.from_label` takes a single label string, so passing the list `['101', '110']` fails. Adding the two single-label statevectors gives a vector with amplitude 1 at index 5 (`|101⟩`) and index 6 (`|110⟩`) and 0 elsewhere. `GroverOperator` turns a `Statevector` oracle into the diagonal `(-1) ** data`, so this flips the phase of both target states and leaves the rest unchanged.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit.quantum_info import Statevector\nfrom qiskit.circuit.library import GroverOperator\n\ntargets = ['101', '110']\n\n# FIX: from_label was given a list but only accepts one label string -> sum the single-label statevectors of each target, because GroverOperator builds the oracle as Diagonal((-1)**data), which flips the phase wherever the entry is 1\noracle = Statevector.from_label(targets[0]) + Statevector.from_label(targets[1])\n\ngrover_op = GroverOperator(oracle)\nprint(grover_op)\n```",
